Author: Wallace Chan <naahtec@hotmail.com>
Date:   Mon Jun 15 09:03:45 2026 -0400

    feat(#12443): harness records activity heartbeat via /hooks/activity
    
    Slice (b) of #12271 (progress-based liveness), harness side. Adds the
    ingestion endpoint + AgentState fields for the activity heartbeat that
    proves the real agent loop is progressing (HARNESS-ARCH §15.1).
    
    - AgentState.last_activity_at (epoch of latest heartbeat) + last_activity
      ({at, event, tool, phase}); persisted in save/load + the manual snapshot.
    - POST /hooks/activity: mirrors /hooks/session-end (X-Agent-Role header,
      unknown/missing-role drop, fail-open always-200). Records the heartbeat
      in-memory immediately (what GET /agents/{role} reads) and THROTTLES the
      state-file write (_ACTIVITY_SAVE_THROTTLE_SECONDS=30) since these fire on
      every tool call — disk staleness within the window is harmless.
    - Exposed via the existing GET /agents/{role}.to_dict().
    
    Observational only (AC5) — does NOT drive the reboot decision yet (#12271
    slice d). TestActivityHook12443 (10 tests); full harness suite green (233).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

